From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:56:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] fix(vk_native): withdraw full side by side in a 2D
 rendering mode

A 2D rendering mode (qwerty's V toggle, or an app's request) hands the
display processor one view, which it passes through. sim_display's own
output setting stays sbs_full then, so the DP still reports
XRT_DP_SCANOUT_FLAG_FULL_SIDE_BY_SIDE, and the declared window kept
twice the width: the single 2D picture was stretched over both views,
its left half shown to the left eye and its right half to the right eye
(measured on the runtime's X11 window after V: both eyes red, view 0).

Count the flag only in a rendering mode with two or more views on a 3D
display state; in a 2D mode the declaration is withdrawn, and it is made
again when a stereo mode returns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>

Origin: vendor, https://github.com/danielcamposramos/displayxr-runtime/commit/2660930fe3644a201ac1c535040d5ee0b552ad47
Forwarded: https://github.com/danielcamposramos/displayxr-runtime/tree/order34-sbs-declare (the pull request to DisplayXR follows the answer on https://github.com/DisplayXR/displayxr-runtime/issues/1928)
Comment: Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 34; made on v2.65.0, applied to v2.66.3 without conflict.
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
---
 docs/reference/xrt_plugin_iface.md                       | 4 +++-
 src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/reference/xrt_plugin_iface.md b/docs/reference/xrt_plugin_iface.md
index c2403c467..d83e38f17 100644
--- a/docs/reference/xrt_plugin_iface.md
+++ b/docs/reference/xrt_plugin_iface.md
@@ -438,7 +438,9 @@ root window (`_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_SUPPORTED`): the runtime sets `_KDE_NET
 = 3 on it, and the window manager keeps the window's place on screen while making the X window
 twice as wide, possibly seconds later. A Vulkan X11 swapchain is always the window's current size,
 so the target becomes two views wide only once the X window is; until then, and after a
-withdrawal, the window is presented at its own size. Where no declaration is offered (another compositor, an app's
+withdrawal, the window is presented at its own size. The flag counts only in a rendering mode with
+two or more views on a 3D display state: a 2D mode (qwerty's V, an app's request) hands the DP one
+view, and the declaration is withdrawn. Where no declaration is offered (another compositor, an app's
 own X11 window, a window manager without the announcement, `DXR_STEREO_DECLARE=0`) the target stays
 the window's size and the runtime logs why in a `FULL_SBS:` line, so the two views show side by
 side, flat. sim_display sets it for `SIM_DISPLAY_OUTPUT=sbs_full` (rendering mode 6, view scale
diff --git a/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c b/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c
index c53f2150a..1349aea7d 100644
--- a/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c
+++ b/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c
@@ -5936,8 +5936,14 @@ vk_full_sbs_refresh_locked(struct comp_vk_native_compositor *c)
 	if (c->display_processor != c->full_sbs.read_dp || idx != c->full_sbs.read_mode_index) {
 		c->full_sbs.read_dp = c->display_processor;
 		c->full_sbs.read_mode_index = idx;
+		// A 2D rendering mode (qwerty's V toggle, an app's request) hands the
+		// DP one view, which it passes through: no stereo pair, whatever the
+		// DP's own output setting is.
+		const struct xrt_rendering_mode *mode =
+		    (c->xdev != NULL && idx < c->xdev->rendering_mode_count) ? &c->xdev->rendering_modes[idx] : NULL;
+		const bool mode_is_stereo = mode == NULL || (mode->hardware_display_3d && mode->view_count >= 2);
 		c->full_sbs.dp_wants =
-		    c->display_processor != NULL &&
+		    c->display_processor != NULL && mode_is_stereo &&
 		    xrt_display_processor_vk_outputs_full_sbs((struct xrt_display_processor_vk *)c->display_processor);
 
 		bool declare = false;
